00:07:26.100 --> 00:07:27.840
The set definitely looks practical

00:07:27.840 --> 00:07:29.525
and that's when you can compare the actual, like,

00:07:29.525 --> 00:07:33.700
the slimy factor and the reflections off of the set to the CG character.

00:07:33.700 --> 00:07:35.100
They're very close.

00:07:35.100 --> 00:07:37.280
The lighting is actually really good on the creatures

00:07:37.280 --> 00:07:42.420
The rendering is pretty good, but I feel like the material doesn't QUITE line up to the set as well.

00:07:42.420 --> 00:07:46.316
The specular highlights are very broad and kind of dim and going across like

00:07:46.316 --> 00:07:47.905
his whole hand there, his face.

00:07:47.905 --> 00:07:51.980
There's another shot where you see like some actual physical prop guts and stuff

00:07:51.980 --> 00:07:54.800
the highlights are way sharper and they're way smaller

00:07:54.800 --> 00:07:55.871
and there's way more of them,

00:07:55.880 --> 00:07:59.120
whereas on the creature they're a little bit dimmer, a little bit more spread out.

00:07:59.120 --> 00:08:00.400
I see what you're saying, totally.

00:08:00.400 --> 00:08:02.580
When you're building like a 3D material,

00:08:02.580 --> 00:08:04.880
generally you're given like a few basic settings

00:08:04.980 --> 00:08:07.320
What's the flat color that you're trying to render?

00:08:07.320 --> 00:08:11.660
Then you can change the specular settings which dictate how reflective certain things can be

00:08:11.670 --> 00:08:14.480
You have another setting for roughness, which is, for instance:

00:08:14.480 --> 00:08:20.260
The roughness of my watch face is basically zero because it's reflecting everything perfectly

00:08:20.360 --> 00:08:25.840
but you have the roughness of maybe this bottle for instance and you see how it's not a flawless pristine reflection.

00:08:25.840 --> 00:08:27.760
There's only so many properties you can tweak

00:08:27.760 --> 00:08:33.320
but when it comes to a character that's covered in blood and dirt and is made out of skin and has a crown,

00:08:33.320 --> 00:08:38.920
you start to get into these situations where you have a lot of these different elements interacting in really unique ways.

00:08:38.920 --> 00:08:44.900
That when you just try and apply like a single texture to a creature you're not able to fully capture what that would actually look like.

00:08:45.300 --> 00:08:47.220
Yeah, but I mean look at that shot there.

00:08:47.220 --> 00:08:52.020
What works in their favor so well is the single point of light right in the center of the scene.

00:08:52.020 --> 00:08:54.820
All of the monsters are actually lit REALLY well.

00:08:54.820 --> 00:08:55.740
Yeah, I love it.

00:08:55.740 --> 00:08:58.400
I'm just saying, like, you're not seeing the right combination

00:08:58.400 --> 00:09:00.840
all these properties trying to be forced into one.

00:09:00.840 --> 00:09:03.660
I– I think a big thing that throws off this effect for me

00:09:03.660 --> 00:09:04.353
is the movement–

00:09:04.360 --> 00:09:05.220
a little too perfect.

00:09:05.420 --> 00:09:07.400
A lot of it feels like it's animated by hand.

00:09:07.800 --> 00:09:10.980
I don't feel like they had a person with, like, a Mocap suit necessarily for this.

00:09:11.180 --> 00:09:13.700
It was more like they filmed someone doing the actions,

00:09:13.780 --> 00:09:15.260
Probably did some paint out,

00:09:15.260 --> 00:09:19.000
and then had someone go in by hand to recreate the character's motion.

00:09:19.000 --> 00:09:22.720
Honestly, like, the monster work in this movie is really solid.

00:09:22.840 --> 00:09:24.460
Yeah. It looks pretty friggin' good to me.

00:09:24.460 --> 00:09:25.860
This is a really cool movie.

00:09:25.860 --> 00:09:26.780
I kind of want to see it.

00:09:26.790 --> 00:09:27.613
I guess it's on YouTube

00:09:27.620 --> 00:09:29.440
and you can just go watch it right now if you want!

00:09:34.860 --> 00:09:36.380
Singham is a great film.

00:09:36.380 --> 00:09:38.300
We've actually gone through this movie before,

00:09:38.300 --> 00:09:41.340
